  - question: Why does it take so long to be diagnosed?
    answer: >-
      Symptoms can be mistaken for normal period pain or other conditions, and
      the only certain test is keyhole surgery. In the UK, it takes on average
      around 8 to 9 years from first symptoms to diagnosis.
  - question: Can I get pregnant with endometriosis?
    answer: >-
      Many people with endometriosis get pregnant without help. Some find it
      harder, and treatments can help.
